<title>UK: Glickman vows to protect US farmers if he has to.</title>
<headline>Glickman vows to protect US farmers if he has to.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman welcomed moves to liberalise the grain trade on Thursday but said he retained the right to use export subsidies to protect American producers if needed.  </p>
<p>Glickman was speaking at a London conference of the International Grains Council.</p>
<p>He welcomed moves to liberalise the grain trading policy of nations such as the European Union, Brazil, Australia and Canada.</p>
<p>But he said that &quot;We retain the right to self defence&quot;.</p>
<p>Glickman said:&quot;I am prepared to use export subsidies to protect US producers&quot;. - - London Newsdesk 00 44 171 542 7729</p>
